{
 "version": "m2_fsw_record v1.3",
 "date": "2026-10-13",
 "sim": "sim6 v2.8-dev (2026-10-13, amendments M, W, F, P, R, S)",
 "method": "What is recorded per base:\n  fsw         the FSW keys as built into the sim6 parameter vector by run6.build (v1.1: values taken from the vector the\n              sim flies, so constants that run6 sets internally are included; keys without a sim6 parameter from the cfg) -\n              the FSW keys of the run6 configuration (guidance, control, estimators, sequencing, detector thresholds and\n              enables, purge sequence), as flown for run 0 of the seed-101 draws (the per-flight calibration inputs are\n              marked: they are set at ARM from measured engine data, the rule is recorded, the run-0 value is an example)\n  fsw_sha16   sha256 (first 16 hex) of the canonical JSON of 'fsw' (sorted keys, floats repr)\n  par_sha16   sha256 of the full sim6 parameter vector of the nominal flight of the base (truth model + FSW), as built by\n              run6.build (identifies the simulator state, not only the FSW)\n  env         GNC_PC_RATCHET as seen by this process and the att_ref_mode it produced (the ratchet is set by\n              os.environ.setdefault in the scripts: RG-13; the record makes the value explicit and checkable)\n  sources     sha16 of sim6.py and run6.py\ncheck(): recomputes fsw_sha16 for a configuration and compares it with the record (raises on a mismatch); scripts and the\nSIL/HIL harness call it before a run. Excluded from 'fsw': truth error injections of the simulator (mest_w, mest_dq, mest_s1,\nmest_s2, the dispersions, the fault and bleed truth models).\nOutput: <out>/fsw_config_record_v1.json",
 "sources": {
  "sim6": "f9094b63e64f2324",
  "run6": "35b5c808487b9339"
 },
 "env": {
  "GNC_PC_RATCHET": "1"
 },
 "per_flight_inputs": {
  "mest_kcal": "1 / measured isp_scale from T1-T4 flow calibration (run-0 value includes the calibration error)",
  "web_kf": "1.1 x a_meas (lead rule, burn limit at t(web = 1 mm))",
  "web_nf1": "n_meas - 0.05",
  "web_nf2": "n_meas + 0.05",
  "web_kcal": "flow calibration as mest_kcal",
  "mest_jref": "nominal-flight J of the cycle",
  "web_jref": "nominal-flight J of the cycle"
 },
 "release_rule_decided": {
  "rule": "release the drogue at E2 AND [measured Pc >= 3.0 bar abs OR the >= 0.8 bar rise held continuously until E2 + 0.10 s]",
  "E2": "relative light confirmation: Pc rise >= 0.8 bar above the pre-lift baseline, held 10 ms (Combustion ignition_detect_v2p4: E2 14.0-15.5 ms after main ignition)",
  "Pc_abs_floor_Pa": 300000.0,
  "rise_Pa": 80000.0,
  "rise_hold_s": 0.01,
  "persistence_timeout_s": 0.1,
  "worst_case_hold_after_E2_s": 0.1,
  "decided": "LEAD 2026-10-13: GNC proposal (b) with the persistence check; a fixed absolute floor alone (proposal (a)) cannot separate lit from unlit at the +/-0.6 bar residual",
  "evidence": "m2_release_rule v1.2 (release_rule.json): release held after the light 0 / 100 / 200 / 400 ms -> pooled A1_none + A1J_pc lost/gained -1/+2, -4/+4, -11/+5 (p 0.21), -21/+6 (p 0.0059); the worst-case hold of this rule (0.10 s) is the P-neutral 100 ms bracket",
  "sim6_status": "amendment R implements 'E2 AND Pc >= 3.0 bar abs' (rel_mode 1; rel_F = map thrust at 3.0 bar abs, run6 DERIVED 37.2 N; rel_dt = E2 after the 6-DOF light). Amendment S implements the persistence branch: rel_to 0.10 s, rise evaluated as the Pc-equivalent thrust >= rel_Frise = map thrust at baseline + 0.8 bar = 2.113 bar abs (ISA 1.013 bar ASSUMED + torch 0.3 bar B-PC-1 target, upper) = 22.9 N; one step below it after E2 loses the branch. m2_bitcheck_v28 v1.5 part S: with the v2.8 thrust ramp the branch never acts (S1: 1000 runs, 0 persistence releases, every stored rel1 value reproduced); with a plateau below 3.0 bar it releases at E2 + 0.10 s (S2); a plateau above 3.0 bar releases on Pc (S3); a plateau below the rise threshold loses the branch (S4). Flown with the plateau in m2_start_transient v1 (RG-01 start-transient re-fly)",
  "flown_in_rev1": "rel_mode 0 (v2.8 model: truth F > 0.5 floor) in every rev1 base except the m2_release_rule arms (rel_mode 1, rel_to 0) and the m2_start_transient arms (rel_mode 1, rel_to 0.10 except arm L400_nto)"
 },
